Technologies Used:
Python
Scikit-learn
NumPy
Jupyter Notebook

Dataset characteristics:
569 samples
30 numerical features
Binary classification
0 → Malignant
1 → Benign

Hidden Layer Architectures Tested:
(50,)
(100,)
(50, 30)
(100, 50)
(100, 50, 25)
(64, 32, 16)

Conclusion:
The results show that increasing the number of layers and neurons does not always improve model performance. 
Moderately sized architectures such as (100,), (50,30), and (64,32,16) achieved the highest accuracy, 
indicating that balanced network complexity can lead to better generalization.

